==============================================================================
1. THE PREDICTION - stated before the numbers, from the decay law
==============================================================================
|c_k| = 2^(r/2) * B_k^(d+1) * |cos(arg z_k)| * 2 / |rho_k|, with
B_k = |1 - 2^(-rho_k)| = sqrt(3/2 - sqrt2 cos(gamma_k log 2)).
B and |cos| are STATIONARY in k; 1/|rho_k| ~ 1/gamma_k is the decay
envelope. Normalisation kills 2^(r/2). The envelope decides the
SHAPE of Neff(N); the stationary modulation only the LEVEL, by a
factor exp(-D) that does not depend on N.

  p_k ~ k^(-s):   s < 1  ->  Neff = (1-s) e^(-s/(1-s)) N   LINEAR
                  s = 1  ->  Neff ~ sqrt(N) log N          SUBLINEAR
                  s > 1  ->  Neff -> finite limit          SATURATES

  gamma_k ~ 2 pi k / log(k/(2 pi e))  =>  s(k) = 1 - 1/log(k/(2 pi e))
  which is BELOW 1 at every finite k and rises to 1 only as k -> inf.

  PREDICTED SHAPE: option 3 - sublinear growth without saturation. Neff(N) rises with local log-log exponent just below 1 across the measured window and does not approach a limit.
  PREDICTED power-law fit over N = 25..600: slope ~ 0.87
  PREDICTED ratio (20,6)/(19,6): flat in N. Neff(20,6)/Neff(19,6) is predicted FLAT in N - both cells share one envelope and both level factors are N-independent - at 1.057 (psi |c|) and 1.095 (pi |c|), and EXACTLY 1.000 at every N on the r-invariant psi |z| profile.

  local log-slope s of gamma_k on the actual zero list:
   k=2..25: 0.5705   k=25..50: 0.6884   k=50..100: 0.7248   k=100..200: 0.7449   k=200..300: 0.7710   k=300..600: 0.7933

