4. WHICH SHAPE - saturating, linear, or sublinear
==============================================================================
Three discriminators, each of which can fire on its own:
  local exponent  b = dlog Neff / dlog N near the top of the range.
                  b -> 0 saturating; b -> 1 linear; 0 < b < 1
                  sublinear.
  Neff/N          constant means linear; falling means sublinear;
                  falling like 1/N means saturating.
  Neff(600)/Neff(300)   1.00 saturating, 2.00 linear, 2.00^b between.

